    "# SynCOM: Synthetic Corona Outflow Model (v3-periodic_blobs)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook runs the Python version of SynCOM step by step. Each function is introduced by a **What it does / expected behaviour** cell: inputs, outputs and what you should see.\n",
    "\n",
    "| section | function |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | `default_syncom_prams` |\n",
    "| 2 | `syncom_load` |\n",
    "| 3 | `syncom_blob_table` |\n",
    "| 4 | `gaussian_profile`, `gaussian_wave` |\n",
    "| 5 | `syncom_image` |\n",
    "| 6 | `syncom_core` |\n",
    "| 7 | `write_fits_frames` |\n",
    "| 8 | `save_syncom_movie` |\n",
    "| 9 | `polar_to_rect`, `plot_rect_image`, `save_rect_movie` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**What's new in v3-periodic_blobs**\n",
    "- **Periodic blobs.** Every blob is launched again each time its period is up, before and during the whole run. The field is equally full at every frame, from the first to the last.\n",
    "- **Launch radius.** A blob begins from its **centre**. It is launched with its centre 6 radial widths below 5 R☉ (the bottom of the polar image), behind the occulter, and slides into the field fully formed. The mean brightness is the same at every radius.\n",
    "- **Speed.** Everything that doesn't change with time (the blob table and the angular profiles) is computed once per run.\n",
    "- **FITS on demand.** `syncom_core` no longer writes a FITS file for every frame. `write_fits_frames` writes only the frames you choose.\n",
    "\n",
    "The tests and the evidence for these changes are in `syncom_notebook_tests.ipynb`.\n"
   ]
