    "# 5. One synthetic image: `syncom_image`\n",
    "\n",
    "## What it does (v3-periodic_blobs)\n",
    "`syncom_image(params, blobs, time_t, gx=None)` (in `syncom_image.py`) builds the image at time step `time_t`, of shape `(NX, NY)`:\n",
    "1. Every blob is **launched once per period**, at $\\tau = \\ldots, -P, 0, P, 2P, \\ldots$ on its own clock $\\tau = t + t_0$. It was already launching before the first frame, and it keeps launching until the last one.\n",
    "2. Each launch begins with its **centre 6 radial widths ($12L$) below 5 R☉**, behind the occulter. It moves outward at the blob's speed $v$, enters the image fully formed, and leaves at the top.\n",
    "3. Each launch is an angular Gaussian (width $L$, periodic) times a radial Gaussian (width $2L$).\n",
    "4. Only launches that have **already happened** and are **still inside the image** are drawn (`launch_range`).\n",
    "5. All blobs are summed, as one matrix product per chunk of 500 blobs. `gx`, the angular part, can be passed in so it's computed once per run.\n",
    "\n",
    "Nothing is written to disk. FITS files are written separately with `write_fits_frames` (section 7).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Expected behaviour\n",
    "- At every position angle with a blob there is a **train of blobs, $v P$ pixels apart**, sliding out from under the occulter.\n",
    "- A new blob centre crosses 5 R☉ every $P$ frames, for every frame of the run. With $P$ = 1 h at a 300 s cadence, that's every 12 frames.\n",
    "- Blobs come out of the occulter fully formed. The mean brightness is the same at every radius from 5 to 14.3 R☉, with no dim ring at the occulter edge (`syncom_notebook_tests.ipynb`, section 3).\n",
